# encoder vs [display], same tick: tier beats patch order.
# Spec: hardware.md §6.12 precedence list, "when more of these events happen at
# the same time ... [display] > Circuit".
#
# The [display] circuit is FIRST in patch order and the encoder SECOND, so the
# plain same-tick tie-break (display.md's "patch order wins, later accepted write
# lands last" — see display/same-tick-tiebreak.gold) would hand the screen to the
# encoder. It must not: a same-tick write is only accepted over an existing owner
# when the writer's tier is >= the owner's, and the circuit tier is below the
# [display] tier.
#
#   t1: I1 changes AND the knob is turned on the same tick.
#       [display] writes 0.7 (owner, tier display, linger 0.01 s = 1 tick),
#       then the encoder attempts 1425 -> same tick, lower tier -> rejected.
#   t2: the display circuit's linger has expired and the encoder is still
#       re-attempting its unchanged pending value -> it lands.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[db8e]

[display]
    value = I1

[encoder]
    encoder      = E1.1
    smooth       = 0
    outputscale  = 2650
    outputoffset = 100
    output       = O1
>>>
@1 set I1 0.7
@1 turn E1.1 48
@1 expectdisplay D1 value 0.7 tol 1e-6
@2 expectdisplay D1 value 1425 tol 1e-3
